{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Kjg7phncezDvSCSXLn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft this, I need a few answers. Your current investors will check the numbers, and two of them stand out:\n\n- **Runway:** At $95,000 a month, $340,000 lasts about 3.5 months, so you have cash until roughly early March. That's before your March–April sales peak.\n- **Profitability:** Your revenue averaged about $35,000 a month, but 70% of it came in two months, so May through August were probably much lower. Burn is $95,000. Saying you'll be profitable next year will only hold up if the update shows how you get there.\n\nMy questions, most important first:\n\n1. **What's the route to profitability?** How many hives under sensor next year, what new revenue, any cost cuts, and in which month do you expect to break even? And what does the $600,000 pay for: how many months, and which milestone should it get you to?\n2. **What are the bridge terms?** SAFE or convertible note, cap and discount, minimum cheque, close date, and how much is already committed (and by whom, if you can say).\n3. **What's your answer to the $45 competitor?** Maybe better detection, the app, your relationships with beekeepers, or something else. Has any customer left, stalled or asked for a lower price since May?\n4. **What evidence goes beyond the one customer?** For example: total hives running sensors, how many of the 31 have renewed or added hives, monthly app revenue, or any comparison of hives with and without sensors in the same operation. Can I name the 4,000-hive customer, and can I quote him?\n5. **Who reads it and who signs it?** How many investors, how they invested (angels or funds), and who signs. Did your last update promise anything they'll remember, like a customer target or a revenue figure?\n6. **What will they learn anyway?** Is there a cost, a missed target, a weak number or a setback I haven't heard about? For instance: revenue since May, a key hire leaving, or production problems.\n\nIf you don't know some of these, say so and I'll write without them rather than guess."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":9573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8033c2eb-7b40-4dfd-a10f-db20e1815e87","uuid":"ad5621b4-463c-47e8-b745-fca40b86b8d3","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:33:49.431Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KjftRmydXApzx3AzPg"}
